      "claim": "Customary international law incorporates the substantive protections of the Fourth Geneva Convention, making them binding on any occupying power regardless of treaty applicability.",
      "reasoning": "Customary IHL has crystallised the core humanitarian protections of the Fourth Geneva Convention, such as the prohibition of forcible transfer of protected persons and the duty to ensure their humane treatment. These rules are considered jus cogens and therefore apply to all states in situations of occupation, even where treaty arguments are raised. Consequently, Israel’s obligations under the Convention are enforceable as customary law in the occupied Palestinian territories.",
      "citations": []
    },
