      "claim": "The International Court of Justice’s advisory opinion on the legal consequences of the construction of a wall in the occupied Palestinian territory confirms that the Fourth Geneva Convention applies to those territories.",
      "reasoning": "In its 2004 advisory opinion, the ICJ examined the status of the territories and concluded that they are occupied territory subject to the Fourth Geneva Convention. The Court’s reasoning rested on the factual situation of military occupation and the existence of an occupying power, not on the question of prior sovereign title. This authoritative pronouncement reinforces the applicability of the Convention to the territories east of the Green Line.",
