      "claim": "Israel’s own ratification of the Fourth Geneva Convention creates an unconditional legal obligation to apply its provisions to any territory it occupies, regardless of the status of the previous sovereign.",
      "reasoning": "Treaty law binds a party to the obligations contained in the treaty in all circumstances covered by the treaty’s scope. By ratifying the Convention, Israel accepted the duty to respect and ensure respect for the Convention’s provisions in any territory it occupies. The treaty’s own text does not provide an exemption for situations where the prior sovereign’s title is disputed; therefore, the Convention’s applicability follows automatically upon the commencement of occupation.",
